  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Justice and Peace Building for Sustainable Communities in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For FY 23 -24 the aim is to contribute to awareness creation, largely for youths, on climate justice/issues of Climate Change (CC) and peacebuilding through a series of online and physical (face to face) engagements. To meet this objective the following activities will be implemented through funding from Oxfam Netherlands (NOVIB):  1) Conducting awareness -raising campaigns about Climate Justice through various media channels: (e.g. social media, community events, workshops) 2) Advocating for policies and practices that promote climate justice and peace building through engagement with policymakers and relevant stakeholders 3) Developing and strengthening partnerships and networks with organizations and individuals working on climate justice and peace building issues 4) Providing training and capacity -building initiatives for vulnerable populations to address climate change and promote peace in their communities 5) Interactive panel discussions with experts, thought leaders, and policymakers to explore current challenges, trends, and best practices in urban mobility and decarbonization. 6) Facilitate capacity building training on environmental issues and skills to enable individuals and organizations to effectively address and respond to environmental challenges 7) Facilitate interactive panel discussions, by bringing together high -level stakeholders and influential individuals to discuss and address pressing societal issues, with a specific focus on the environment 8) Conduct social media campaign to raise awareness of youth, fostering engagement, and promoting action on various climate -related issues</narrative>
  </description>
